  Midas Core System

Midas Core is a Spring Boot-based financial transaction processing microservice. It receives transactions from Kafka, validates and stores them in a PostgreSQL database, and forwards relevant data to an external REST API for incentives.


---

🚀 Tech Stack

Java 17

Spring Boot

Apache Kafka

PostgreSQL

Docker & Docker Compose



---

📦 Project Structure

Kafka Integration: KafkaTransactionListener, KafkaConsumerConfig

Database Layer: Transaction, TransactionRepository

Service Layer: TransactionService

API Client: RestTemplate bean

Utils: SampleKafkaProducer for test data



---

⚙️ Setup Instructions

1. Prerequisites

Java 17+

Maven or Gradle

Docker & Docker Compose


2. Clone the Repository

git clone <repo-url>
cd midas-core

3. Start Kafka, Zookeeper, and PostgreSQL

docker-compose up -d

4. Configure Application

Edit application.properties if needed:

spring.datasource.url=jdbc:postgresql://localhost:5432/midasdb
spring.datasource.username=midas
spring.datasource.password=midaspass

5. Run the Application

./mvnw spring-boot:run

6. Send a Sample Kafka Message

Run SampleKafkaProducer to simulate a transaction:

mvn compile exec:java -Dexec.mainClass="com.midas.core.util.SampleKafkaProducer"


---

📡 REST API Integration

The TransactionService sends processed transactions to a REST API endpoint:

POST http://incentive-api/notify

Make sure this API is available or mocked during local testing.


